  "fanTake": "Well, that's what we call a weekend we'd all like back. A 10-13 loss to Seattle is the kind of game that stings precisely because it feels winnable—we were right there, we just couldn't quite finish the job. The offense sputtered (negative EPA per play will do that), the defense gave up a red zone touchdown they shouldn't have, and we coughed up the football three times to their zero. It's tough to win football games when you're beating yourself like that, and it's tougher still when you're about to face the next four weeks without your most explosive receiving target."
